From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:53:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: record patches 166 to 178 in the stack manifest

Phase P4 of the IndexedDB redesign: getAll() options, getAllRecords()
and IDBRecord (166); a store record's key read once (167); the store
rows kept in the database actor, a put's index keys checked and stored
with one statement per table, the key generator written once per
transaction and RDB's NULL check only for empty blobs (168 to 171, fork
files only, tier A); cursor prefetch (172); keyPath returning the same
Array, IDBObjectStore.index() throwing once an abort has started, keys
computed from a clone without page code, a pref that exposes
SharedArrayBuffer for tests, and SharedArrayBuffers and views on them as
binary keys (173 to 177). The test pref (176) is a seam, a default-off
pref and two lines in the global creation, and is tier B like comparable
script-behaviour patches; the other script changes are C, and this
bookkeeping entry is B, like the earlier ones.

The P4 review fixes are folded into entries 172 (the byte bound of a
cursor step's records, write counts per object store, kept records
dropped when the transaction finishes), 176 (the pref renamed
js_shared_memory_enabled_for_testing and documented as test-only) and
177; the patches were regenerated after that rewrite.

Validation: `uv run docs/ohos-sync/check_stack.py base/2026-11-09` passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, with the patches generated by gen_patches.py and regenerated after folding the P4 review fixes)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
